{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod","id":1410879,"title":"Incentive Mechanics - Momentum for CoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-28T13:46:35-07:00","id":1410879,"title":"Incentive Mechanics - Momentum for CoD?","content":"I run various games of <b>CoD</b> 1E and 2E for 15+ years now. Lately, I ran also two chronicles in <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> and few sessions of games in <b>Storypath</b> engines \u2013 and I found <b>CoD</b> rules <i>really</i> static to those games. There is no feel of dynamism in <b>CoD</b> rules. \ud83d\ude14 No real feel of \u2018risk or reward\u2019 in play. Just static \u2018you can make something dangerous and get extra beat/XP for that\u2019. It\u2019s\u2026 slow, in gameplay. There is\u2026 no incentive to risk for extra game fun.<br /> <br /> Here comes <b>Storypath</b> Momentum ( or <b>Realms of Pugmire </b>Fortune ). Those are piles of points/counters that let you make rerolls, extra narrative element or other stuff. Players generate them in play by deliberating failures in throws. Somehow similar mechanics is in <b>CoD</b> 2E with getting Dramatic Failure \u2013 but the reward is just \u2018I get extra small XP(beat)\u2019 \u2013 nothing in the game or game narrative itself. With Momentum, it would like \u2018We have extra point to reroll or add narrative element to use later in session\u2019.<br /> <br /> For example, I run <b>Werewolf</b> chronicle now. Players are rather omitting risking even Soft Rage \u2013 in <b>WtF</b> 2E I found mechanics of Rage Triggers somehow not working to full potential. Players are choosing 3 individual and few general ones \u2013 but on day to day basis, Triggers do not lend even to start of Soft Rage scene. How it would much cooler to say to player: \u2018You do not have this as your Trigger, but if you go for it, you will get extra Momentum. It\u2019s Soft Rage scene, you surely will handle it\u2026\u2019 \ud83d\ude08<br /> <br /> To make it more tempting, all the left Momentum after the session could become extra Beat \u2013 or even full XP for whole party. Or that Momentum point can reactivate used \u2018once per session\u2019 one power, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>What do you think about idea like this?</b> What usage of Momentum in <b>CoD</b> games could you find then?<br /> <br /> I summon <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> as guru on <b>Storypath </b>engine. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T14:23:34-07:00","id":1410884,"title":"","content":"First, there's a different in tone of game to consider. The CofD is a horror/urban fantasy game, getting too far into how RoP or StoryPath encourage high adventure risks mucking with the atmosphere of the game. <br /> <br /> Second, your analysis seems to completely skip Willpower: both what it does (be a general pool to spend on doing stuff better), and how to get it back (mostly adding complications to your character's lives). With Beats and Willpower, there's already a lot of incentive mechanics in the CofD.<br /> <br /> Also, please, do not do the &quot;Momentum into XP&quot; idea. That has the opposite effect where players will hoard it rather than spend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T15:20:48-07:00","id":1410890,"title":"","content":"Agree with most of what Heavy Arms said, it\u2019s a different tone and willpower do most of the job of momentum. Definitely exchanging left over momentum for beats is not a good idea, actually would make it worse.<br /> <br /> What willpower miss from momentum is the \u201cgain points for doing things you suck at\u201d. Gaining momentum for failing, 2 momentum for botch and extra momentum if a condition make it harder is a real thing in Storypath and give some extra reason to risk.<br /> <br /> Honestly never played WtF, and it\u2019s probably the one that I read least about, but it seams it\u2019s one of the most action focused of the CoD, and maybe some momentum could help to make the game move on a more racing way. You could add momentum as a group resource, as happen in Storypath, or you could make an individual \u201crage pool\u201d that fills with botches, failures and conditions, and is spent by adding dice to rolls. The rage pool could store no more than 5 point and if in the end of the session the character has no more than 1 point he gains an extra XP.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know, maybe you can link it to some other effects, to make it interesting to keep it low, like a \u201chunger dice\u201d mechanic (from V5), when you have too much rage you become unpredictable (messy criticals and failures), so it become an strategy, to keep it high to spend it in the right moments or to spend it soon to keep controlled.<br /> <br /> If you like the idea we can discuss more about it, I am willing to use Hungry Dice in my games but don\u2019t know how to yet... probably on Aberrant... Maybe Werewolf could be an interesting place to use, with all the fury and hunt.<br /> <br /> Thank for the guru title, but there is only one and she is Danielle, I am no more than an admirer of a great job they did on the system. Feel free to summon, though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T15:38:18-07:00","id":1410895,"title":"","content":"Willpower doesn't give you points for doing things you suck at mostly because the Conditions/Beats cycle get that design space.<br /> <br /> For Forsaken specifically in 2e, it's a game about hunting. Hunting is something that it supposed to have a slow burn until it explodes into brief violence rather than the cinematic back and forth of trading blows Storypath aims for by giving Momentum for missing attacks. The Uratha are really potent, but they're designed to utilize their pre-built-in synergies and team work rather than Zerg rushing enemies into oblivion. I'm not sure what adding a Momentum like mechanic would do for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T17:19:43-07:00","id":1410905,"title":"","content":"As a very crass comparison, I like both Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd Edition and Tenra Bansho Zero as expressions of physical violence, but I wouldn't use TBZ's &quot;Every attack can be counter-attacked&quot; base system for Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Momentum's fun, but it clashes with Forsaken's sensiblities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T23:49:45-07:00","id":1410956,"title":"","content":"Maybe I will limit analysis to <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>, as I really fought of this for this game specifically, on first thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410884#post1410884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, there's a different in tone of game to consider. The CofD is a horror/urban fantasy game, getting too far into how RoP or StoryPath encourage high adventure risks mucking with the atmosphere of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree. Maybe on general <b>CoD</b> games, probably yes, but most <b>Werewolf</b>-related horror movies are high action packed. I just watched like 5 movies from last 20 years or so, for game research. They are all a bit action packed, one way or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410884#post1410884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, your analysis seems to completely skip Willpower: both what it does (be a general pool to spend on doing stuff better), and how to get it back (mostly adding complications to your character's lives). With Beats and Willpower, there's already a lot of incentive mechanics in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower as resources is like\u2026 good thing 15 years ago. I found it usable in mortal games, maybe <b>Hunter</b> gameline \u2013 but in <b>Werewolf</b> you have Essence first, Beats later. <b>Willpower</b> is almost forgetful \u2013 at least in <b>WtF</b> 2E I run now 4 years, Willpower is almost not needed for players to start powers \u2013 and in in any case, when they need to equalize the pot with the opponent - it is enough to sleep off or one or two scenes of role-playing. It doesn't get any great excitement.<br /> <br /> Willpower does a little bit of nothing about the <b>Werewolf</b>, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And burning it for Soft and Hard Rage tests misses the point of these mechanics.<br /> <br /> And Beats, as I pointed above, are really \u2018yep, I will hoard them at the end of the game, cool\u2019 \u2013 nothing really changing in dramatic atmosphere \u2018now, in the game\u2019. After the time it\u2019s like \u2018we get 3 or 4 Beats? Cool\u2019, you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410884#post1410884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, please, do not do the &quot;Momentum into XP&quot; idea. That has the opposite effect where players will hoard it rather than spend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is probably good idea. <b>Momentum should be only for particular session, story at most to be spend \u2013 or lost then.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T23:58:58-07:00","id":1410957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410890#post1410890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What willpower miss from momentum is the \u201cgain points for doing things you suck at\u201d. Gaining momentum for failing, 2 momentum for botch and extra momentum if a condition make it harder is a real thing in Storypath and give some extra reason to risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly this. Beats ( so XP ) fill this niche in <b>CoD</b>, but it\u2019s too static in my gameplay experience. Momentum gives MUCH more dramatism to game, in my observation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410890#post1410890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What You could add momentum as a group resource, as happen in Storypath, or you could make an individual \u201crage pool\u201d that fills with botches, failures and conditions, and is spent by adding dice to rolls. The rage pool could store no more than 5 point and if in the end of the session the character has no more than 1 point he gains an extra XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Individual Rage Pool is to consider, but I would much more go with Group Momentum, like in <b>Storypath</b>, because of two things:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Werewolves are group monsters \u2013 Pack is <i>literally</i> everything to them.</li> <li>I wanted Momentum to not only reflect the Rage of individual \u2013 but also adding narrative elements to the game. Like showing Contacts or possible Mentor outside of Merits list, or simply characters possibility to rerolls dicepools \u2013 not only adding merely +3 from Willpower. BIG THINGS in the gameplay.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-29-2020, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T00:12:45-07:00","id":1410960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410890#post1410890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly never played WtF, and it\u2019s probably the one that I read least about, but it seams it\u2019s one of the most action focused of the CoD, and maybe some momentum could help to make the game move on a more racing way.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410895#post1410895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower For Forsaken specifically in 2e, it's a game about hunting. Hunting is something that it supposed to have a slow burn until it explodes into brief violence rather than the cinematic back and forth of trading blows Storypath aims for by giving Momentum for missing attacks. The Uratha are really potent, but they're designed to utilize their pre-built-in synergies and team work rather than Zerg rushing enemies into oblivion. I'm not sure what adding a Momentum like mechanic would do for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree with <b>Heavy Arms</b>. Yes,<b> WtF</b> 2E is about Hunt. Yes, Uratha ( werewolves ) are to be greatest predators. BUT, story of the Hunt is <b><i>always</i></b> story about rise and falls of hunters to find and get their prey. If it would be only \u2018our best strategy wins the Hunt in one strike\u2019 \u2013 it\u2019s not a story, it\u2019s simply one, two scene. It would be not 2,5 hour movie \u2013 only 15 minutes \u2018we do this, that, and get our target\u2019. Remember \u2018Princess Mononoke\u2019. Remember \u2018The Ghost and Darkness\u2019 \u2013 hunters there <i><u>failed</u></i> to make story interesting. <b>Stories of Hunt are made from rise and falls of hunters. Mechanics of rise and fall of Momentum are better representing this than static \u2018you gets X Bears/XP at the end of game\u2019.</b><br /> <br /> To see more, just see TV Tropes: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BigTropeHunting\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...igTropeHunting</a><br /> <br /> ( BTW, I do not plan to ax Beats mechanics entirely for the game \u2013 I just want to make <b>CoD</b> mechanic a bit much more like Sotrypath \u2013 where Momentum makes game tension, and XP are general character development. )<br /> <br /> Also, in <b>WtF</b> 2E we <b><i>already</i></b> have similar mechanics to Momentum \u2013 it\u2019s called <i>Tension Pool</i>, and is in the <i>First Change Story</i> scenario in the corebook ( p. 291 ). It\u2019s limited only to the pre-First Change mortals-to-Uratha \u2013 but it\u2019s point it\u2019s intrinsic element of the Hunt stories, also. I just like Momentum on general being a bit better in the gameplay, more open ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T00:25:35-07:00","id":1410963,"title":"","content":"Okay, no the meat of the idea \u2013 <b>How to implement Storypath Momentum to CoD 2E mechanics? </b>( You can have in mind we talk here about <b>Werewolf the Forsaken </b>2E, specifically ) I do want to keep Beats for general character development ( <b>Storypath</b> doing the same, only called as general XP ), but want the Momentum to rise and fall in the game, to add this gameplay flow of <b>Storypath</b>.<br /> <br /> My starting idea on Momentum generation:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Momentum is added on Dramatic Failures ( DF from now ). Players still get 1 Beat from each DF, but the Momentum rise by 1. Players still can declare they take Dramatic Failure and get Momentum from this.</li> <li>Players can get Momentum for willingly making their situation worse \u2013 like testing Soft Rage from Trigger outside of their list. ( Need more examples on this. \ud83d\ude10 )</li> <li>Conditions still gets only Beats for the characters.</li> <li>Storyteller introducing extra threat in the scene and players agree.</li> <li>Other Momentum sources?</li> </ol>What can Momentum be used for:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Reroll one test</li> <li>Add narrative element to the game \u2013 like new NPC showing up, players generally describes it, Storyteller makes rest of his details and stats.</li> </ol>That\u2019s what I have for now, really\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T00:48:18-07:00","id":1410965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410957#post1410957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Individual Rage Pool is to consider, but I would much more go with Group Momentum, like in <b>Storypath</b>, because of two things:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Werewolves are group monsters \u2013 Pack is <i>literally</i> everything to them.</li> <li>I wanted Momentum to not only reflect the Rage of individual \u2013 but also adding narrative elements to the game. Like showing Contacts or possible Mentor outside of Merits list, or simply characters possibility to rerolls dicepools \u2013 not only adding merely +3 from Willpower. BIG THINGS in the gameplay.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point, the idea of the pack is really good.<br /> Looks like you want more than just momentum, you want to give some narrative power to the players, like Path Uses and Rewrites. It\u2019s a bit more than just Momentum and the impact would be bigger.<br /> Maybe adding the Paths to the game and let them use it as a narrative resource, but it would conflict with some merits, like you said, Contacts, Mentor and maybe more.<br /> With less impact, you could use the Cinematics from TCF, spending Momentum to do some crazy stuff, it can be less crazy, as the focus is less comic, but some major effect yet. You can even combine with the Stunts from TCF (but costing Momentum to use) issue here is, if you don\u2019t have some \u201carchetype\u201d characteristic to lock it (in Werewolf it could be the Augur, maybe), the stunts get a bit too generic.<br /> <br /> I would try to go for the latter, as it has less impact on the charactera as written, pick some cinematics and stunts from TCF, let them use in exchange from momentum, and see if the game flows as expected.<br /> <br /> Edit: I have written this while you were writing the last 2 posts, so it may sound redundant to your posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-29-2020, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T06:40:23-07:00","id":1410991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410956#post1410956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe on general <b>CoD</b> games, probably yes, but most <b>Werewolf</b>-related horror movies are high action packed. I just watched like 5 movies from last 20 years or so, for game research. They are all a bit action packed, one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf the Forsaken is not a &quot;werewolf movie simulator.&quot; And even if we are to look at werewolf cinema in general, werewolf movies are high in violence, but low in action. That is, the werewolf/werewolves kill a lot of people, but it's generally brief violent attacks on normal folks, and the only big action scenes tends towards the climax of the film as the werewolf hunters finally force a confrontation with the hunting werewolf/werewolves.<br /> <br /> Hell, the book lists An American Werewolf in London as inspiration. There isn't a single scene in the whole movie that would justify breaking out the full combat rules for. Everything is effectively a Down &amp; Dirty combat roll off, if you'd even bother rolling it. Werewolf!David only attacks normal people that don't stand a chance. The final scene has <b>eight</b> police officers with assault rifles aiming on him to gun him down; he was never fighting his way out of that alley. This was &quot;the&quot; werewolf movie formula for decades: character gets bitten by werewolf and becomes one, character struggles to control their violent urges, eventually someone kills them after they fail to keep it controlled.<br /> <br /> Forsaken avoids this archetypal plot because it would be exceedingly bad for a game where you want to play your character for any sort of extended amount of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Willpower</b> is almost forgetful \u2013 at least in <b>WtF</b> 2E I run now 4 years, Willpower is almost not needed for players to start powers \u2013 and in in any case, when they need to equalize the pot with the opponent - it is enough to sleep off or one or two scenes of role-playing. It doesn't get any great excitement. </div> </div> </div>It feels really strange to want something like Momentum, which is easy to gain so you spend it freely (and even has rules specifically to discourage players from hoarding it) but gives a relatively simple default boost to rolls.... and then say that the problem with Willpower is that it's too easy to get so it's never interesting.<br /> <br /> IMO... players spend WP all the time precisely because there's no point to holding on to it when you can regain it as easily as you can as an Uratha. If a major scene doesn't end with all the players down to half their WP at a minimum, we'd be very confused about why such a major scene was so easy and/or dismissed as not worth tossing lots of WP at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And burning it for Soft and Hard Rage tests misses the point of these mechanics. </div> </div> </div>This makes no sense. How is spending WP to help prolong and/or control Rage for an action missing the point of anything?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410960#post1410960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT, story of the Hunt is <b><i>always</i></b> story about rise and falls of hunters to find and get their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... make sure the to have difficult hunts in your games where failure is a possibility either for specific parts of the hunt that can be recovered from, or flat out failing them. <br /> <br /> Momentum isn't going have more failures during hunts just by adding it to the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanics of rise and fall of Momentum are better representing this than static \u2018you gets X Bears/XP at the end of game\u2019. </div> </div> </div>Not really? Momentum is good at representing lots of little failures helping to built up to a big success, not a constant ebb and flow of success/failure. <br /> <br /> How Forsaken has worked for me, is that the big hunts that are the core of a given story are difficult enough for the PCs that they spend way more WP than they can recover by resting, so they're actually tempted to grab for all the Willpower regain stuff that involves adding so setbacks or negative consequences to the story to get enough WP back to keep going.<br /> <br /> It really sounds to me like your problem is that you're going too easy on your players (esp. the idea that they're forgetting about WP completely) than the WP and Beats incentive cycles don't work if you put them too work (Momentum is equally subject to GMs not getting the balance right of making sure the players get enough to do cool things, but not too much that they're not looking to gain more when they can).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To see more, just see TV Tropes: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BigTropeHunting\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...igTropeHunting</a> </div> </div> </div>This big list of things tells us nothing about what you're trying to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410879-incentive-mechanics-momentum-for-cod?p=1410963#post1410963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]<br /> What can Momentum be used for: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Reroll one test</li> <li>Add narrative element to the game \u2013 like new NPC showing up, players generally describes it, Storyteller makes rest of his details and stats.</li> </ol><br /> That\u2019s what I have for now, really\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is, really, the problem.<br /> <br /> If all Momentum can do is a reroll or a moment of director stance... it's not worth the headaches or trying to weld Momentum in. It's better to just do something like allow WP to do limited Dramatic Editing for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T12:25:03-07:00","id":1411016,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Try to keep the posts in one big post, Wyrhammer.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T13:16:22-07:00","id":1411019,"title":"","content":"The idea of a more flexible Willpower is interesting. Probably better than adding momentum, as there are enough resources in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T14:58:44-07:00","id":1411027,"title":"","content":"More flexible WP just needs to be careful because that's already the core bonus for Hunters (though not something like Dramatic Editing) that doesn't require investing in Endowments or Tactics.<br /> <br /> It doesn't look like it would be hard to navigate, but it should get a bit of attention to make sure Hunters don't feel diminished, or that Hunters don't get an unintended buff.<br /> <br /> My first instincts are two options:<br /> <br /> 1) Flat edit in terms of how big of an impact it has, with a flat cost of 2 WP, Hunters can do it with 1 WP, but don't get to do anything else with their WP expenditure.<br /> <br /> 2) Scaled edit with scaled WP costs. Hunters reduce the WP cost by 1 with the same caveat above, unless the reduction would be to zero, where they still spend WP, but can also get their normal extra options; basically turning level 1 edits into another option Hunters can pick from when spending WP.<br /> <br /> It might get a bit meta for some people, as it would feel like Hunters are literally willing the world into helping them keep their vigils if not treated as a purely player decision, but for the goal of adding some extra player control over scenarios it seems the easiest way to integrate it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T15:50:19-07:00","id":1411028,"title":"","content":"Hm, if anything.<br /> Tension is the mechanic that might work better conceptually speaking to port over.<br /> Although it wouldnt be as easy as momentum to transfer over to CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T00:24:38-08:00","id":1475483,"title":"","content":"If WP doesn't work as your source of dramatic editing, you could always implement stunts from Exalted, but give them a horror twist. So, when you do something dangerous and violent, you get +2 dice, which can be used immediately, saved for a similar roll later on, or spent for a dramatic edit. It's a bit less 'willing the world to work this way', and more of a reward for sticking to the theme/genre.<br /> <br /> You also have extra successes on your rolls that could be saved in the same way, if you want that instead. Let's say you roll three successes. You only need one to succeed, so you could save the other two to spend on dramatic editing at the right time instead of getting an immediate benefit on the current roll (risk versus reward, as you wanted). You'd need to decide what dramatic editing costs (two saved successes sounds about right, but you could have a scaling cost, as Heavy Arms suggests).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T11:42:23-08:00","id":1475500,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I define necromancy as basically resurrecting any posts older than a year and usually over six months without a response. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}